{"id": "I1", "section": "Discussion", "text": "Prompt engineering is defined consistently as designing instructions to guide model output without altering model parameters, and one source adds that prompts can also be seen as a form of programming.", "premises": ["C1", "C2", "C3", "C10"], "verdicts": [{"question_id": "paper.inference_follows", "answer": false, "probabilities": null, "confidence": 0.8, "confidence_source": "self_report", "backend": "glm-flash", "escalated": true, "cost_usd": 3.6685e-05, "latency_ms": 4469, "trace_id": "f8d057ba1d57402fa721d1d9b4577c35", "producer_id": "p3.paper.interpret", "judge_id": "p2.judge"}, {"question_id": "paper.inference_follows", "answer": true, "probabilities": null, "confidence": 0.62, "confidence_source": "self_report", "backend": "sonnet-ref", "escalated": false, "cost_usd": 0.006508, "latency_ms": 5883, "trace_id": "4e48ca0165f749268a280c3a7281b962", "producer_id": "p3.paper.interpret", "judge_id": "p2.judge"}], "status": "pass", "reason": "unsettled at write time: the reference judge was unsure"}
{"id": "I2", "section": "Discussion", "text": "The prompt-engineering field is nonetheless described as having conflicting terminology and a fragmented understanding of what makes a prompt effective, and practitioners' skill is called loosely defined, so the consistent definition coexists with an unsettled vocabulary.", "premises": ["C12", "C14", "C1"], "verdicts": [{"question_id": "paper.inference_follows", "answer": true, "probabilities": null, "confidence": 0.95, "confidence_source": "self_report", "backend": "glm-flash", "escalated": true, "cost_usd": 2.1982e-05, "latency_ms": 2644, "trace_id": "7a2ee8f007e148fea4bb32646e1139d8", "producer_id": "p3.paper.interpret", "judge_id": "p2.judge"}], "status": "pass", "reason": null}
{"id": "I3", "section": "Discussion", "text": "Context engineering is framed in two compatible ways: as a shift from input-level linguistic control to system-level orchestration, and as adapting inputs with instructions, strategies or evidence rather than weight updates.", "premises": ["C51", "C18", "C16"], "verdicts": [{"question_id": "paper.inference_follows", "answer": true, "probabilities": null, "confidence": 0.9, "confidence_source": "self_report", "backend": "glm-flash", "escalated": true, "cost_usd": 2.01318e-05, "latency_ms": 1493, "trace_id": "03dd08d729894b5eb98488e6d3000244", "producer_id": "p3.paper.interpret", "judge_id": "p2.judge"}], "status": "pass", "reason": null}
{"id": "I4", "section": "Discussion", "text": "Several claims attach concrete concerns to context: exceeding the usable window forces decisions about discarding history, and context growth is linked to degraded reasoning and tool-calling reliability.", "premises": ["C4", "C22"], "verdicts": [{"question_id": "paper.inference_follows", "answer": true, "probabilities": {"true": 0.77, "false": 0.22999999999999998}, "confidence": 0.77, "confidence_source": "logprobs", "backend": "jev", "escalated": false, "cost_usd": 2.4863999999999998e-05, "latency_ms": 136, "trace_id": "41e77121f3714f18a5b8da30df53c0e7", "producer_id": "p3.paper.interpret", "judge_id": "p2.judge"}], "status": "pass", "reason": null}
{"id": "I5", "section": "Discussion", "text": "The harness is described as the external execution support structure built around the model, treated as a first-class object of design, evaluation, and optimization. The Code as Agent Harness survey draws the boundary with earlier stages by saying that prompt engineering changes instructions and context engineering changes what evidence is presented, whereas harness engineering treats the operating environment itself as the object of analysis.", "premises": ["C25", "C7", "C43"], "verdicts": [{"question_id": "paper.inference_follows", "answer": false, "probabilities": null, "confidence": 0.7, "confidence_source": "self_report", "backend": "glm-flash", "escalated": true, "cost_usd": 0.000155265, "latency_ms": 15520, "trace_id": "50ef4f86d496480aadc6e9ca3b82374a", "producer_id": "p3.paper.interpret", "judge_id": "p2.judge"}, {"question_id": "paper.inference_follows", "answer": false, "probabilities": null, "confidence": 0.8, "confidence_source": "self_report", "backend": "sonnet-ref", "escalated": false, "cost_usd": 0.00447, "latency_ms": 2777, "trace_id": "c8ed3460e7114462ae804c67f03565b2", "producer_id": "p3.paper.interpret", "judge_id": "p2.judge"}, {"question_id": "paper.inference_follows", "answer": true, "probabilities": null, "confidence": 0.95, "confidence_source": "self_report", "backend": "glm-flash", "escalated": true, "cost_usd": 2.668275e-05, "latency_ms": 5277, "trace_id": "37e71e66c9d54e5b9bd3bf22b382824b", "producer_id": "p3.paper.interpret", "judge_id": "p2.judge"}], "status": "pass", "reason": null}
{"id": "I6", "section": "Discussion", "text": "The claims place the stages relative to one another in different ways. The externalization review calls the harness's separation of the prompt into layers a structured form of context engineering, which places the harness partly inside context engineering. The Code as Agent Harness survey instead presents harness engineering as a separate stage whose object of analysis is the operating environment. The harness-engineering survey describes a boundary that shifts as routine capability-bearing support migrates into model weights while constraint-bearing governance functions stay external.", "premises": ["C20", "C43", "C32"], "verdicts": [{"question_id": "paper.inference_follows", "answer": false, "probabilities": null, "confidence": 0.85, "confidence_source": "self_report", "backend": "glm-flash", "escalated": true, "cost_usd": 2.668e-05, "latency_ms": 7773, "trace_id": "1f3d2eb481c9484abd663735ca7f0561", "producer_id": "p3.paper.interpret", "judge_id": "p2.judge"}, {"question_id": "paper.inference_follows", "answer": false, "probabilities": null, "confidence": 0.7, "confidence_source": "self_report", "backend": "sonnet-ref", "escalated": false, "cost_usd": 0.006246, "latency_ms": 4556, "trace_id": "abd74182029a441cbb2f20a818db59c2", "producer_id": "p3.paper.interpret", "judge_id": "p2.judge"}, {"question_id": "paper.inference_follows", "answer": true, "probabilities": null, "confidence": 0.85, "confidence_source": "self_report", "backend": "glm-flash", "escalated": true, "cost_usd": 6.027e-05, "latency_ms": 13255, "trace_id": "7d10a33b49dc40798334ea9bf9b5b1b1", "producer_id": "p3.paper.interpret", "judge_id": "p2.judge"}], "status": "pass", "reason": null}
{"id": "I7", "section": "Discussion", "text": "Components attributed to the harness layer include memory, a context constructor, skill routing, an orchestration loop and verification and governance, as well as sandboxes, evaluators and approval loops.", "premises": ["C26", "C36", "C34"], "verdicts": [{"question_id": "paper.inference_follows", "answer": true, "probabilities": null, "confidence": 0.9, "confidence_source": "self_report", "backend": "glm-flash", "escalated": true, "cost_usd": 2.30463e-05, "latency_ms": 1611, "trace_id": "911f3d843c404775a253ae2fbeb5e4c8", "producer_id": "p3.paper.interpret", "judge_id": "p2.judge"}], "status": "pass", "reason": null}
{"id": "I8", "section": "Discussion", "text": "The evaluation claims matter because changing the execution system around a fixed model can alter performance and reverse rankings, so a score reflects a model–harness–environment configuration rather than the model alone.", "premises": ["C6", "C45", "C47"], "verdicts": [{"question_id": "paper.inference_follows", "answer": true, "probabilities": null, "confidence": 0.9, "confidence_source": "self_report", "backend": "glm-flash", "escalated": true, "cost_usd": 3.48e-05, "latency_ms": 13617, "trace_id": "ce6857e080634164b2d909b4004e6e48", "producer_id": "p3.paper.interpret", "judge_id": "p2.judge"}], "status": "pass", "reason": null}
{"id": "I9", "section": "Conclusions", "text": "The claims support a layered account in which prompt engineering concerns instructions, context engineering concerns what evidence and history the model sees, and harness engineering concerns the surrounding execution environment.", "premises": ["C43", "C1", "C16"], "verdicts": [{"question_id": "paper.inference_follows", "answer": true, "probabilities": null, "confidence": 0.9, "confidence_source": "self_report", "backend": "glm-flash", "escalated": true, "cost_usd": 2.9763e-05, "latency_ms": 8952, "trace_id": "25e4628b10164755b863bc21c2ca0ca2", "producer_id": "p3.paper.interpret", "judge_id": "p2.judge"}], "status": "pass", "reason": null}
{"id": "I10", "section": "Conclusions", "text": "Retrieval, memory, tool use, orchestration and evaluation or verification loops are attributed mostly to the harness and agentic layers, though the claims do not assign each component to one stage exclusively.", "premises": ["C26", "C36", "C5", "C34"], "verdicts": [{"question_id": "paper.inference_follows", "answer": true, "probabilities": null, "confidence": 0.8, "confidence_source": "self_report", "backend": "glm-flash", "escalated": true, "cost_usd": 3.12098e-05, "latency_ms": 4668, "trace_id": "ab7d22b167d74ba3b16647a3ef468b68", "producer_id": "p3.paper.interpret", "judge_id": "p2.judge"}], "status": "pass", "reason": null}
{"id": "I11", "section": "Conclusions", "text": "Boundaries between context engineering and harness engineering are not settled, since the claims offer both a nesting view and a separation view.", "premises": ["C20", "C43"], "verdicts": [{"question_id": "paper.inference_follows", "answer": true, "probabilities": null, "confidence": 0.85, "confidence_source": "self_report", "backend": "glm-flash", "escalated": true, "cost_usd": 2.15673e-05, "latency_ms": 2484, "trace_id": "f152fdc820a9469fab055c06d071a166", "producer_id": "p3.paper.interpret", "judge_id": "p2.judge"}], "status": "pass", "reason": null}
{"id": "I12", "section": "Conclusions", "text": "The claims do not show that any one architecture is best, and they leave open a common account of why memory, skills and protocols converge.", "premises": ["C38", "C52"], "verdicts": [{"question_id": "paper.inference_follows", "answer": true, "probabilities": null, "confidence": 0.95, "confidence_source": "self_report", "backend": "glm-flash", "escalated": true, "cost_usd": 1.760175e-05, "latency_ms": 6310, "trace_id": "5d365261bdb2495fa3ab58221acc741f", "producer_id": "p3.paper.interpret", "judge_id": "p2.judge"}], "status": "pass", "reason": null}
{"id": "I13", "section": "A research agenda", "text": "Compare the competing boundary definitions on a shared corpus to test whether prompt, context and harness engineering can be separated consistently.", "premises": ["C12", "C20", "C43"], "verdicts": [{"question_id": "paper.inference_follows", "answer": true, "probabilities": null, "confidence": 0.85, "confidence_source": "self_report", "backend": "glm-flash", "escalated": true, "cost_usd": 2.1663e-05, "latency_ms": 3519, "trace_id": "5a7e33bfac064899a4d4cc160118acb9", "producer_id": "p3.paper.interpret", "judge_id": "p2.judge"}], "status": "pass", "reason": null}
{"id": "I14", "section": "A research agenda", "text": "Evaluate agents with harness configurations, budgets and scoring procedures reported in standardised form and with the model held fixed, to measure how much rankings depend on the harness.", "premises": ["C54", "C6", "C45"], "verdicts": [{"question_id": "paper.inference_follows", "answer": true, "probabilities": null, "confidence": 0.85, "confidence_source": "self_report", "backend": "glm-flash", "escalated": true, "cost_usd": 2.4853e-05, "latency_ms": 5195, "trace_id": "5309d4c208254ac49f66a642768d1719", "producer_id": "p3.paper.interpret", "judge_id": "p2.judge"}], "status": "pass", "reason": null}
{"id": "I15", "section": "A research agenda", "text": "Extend context-management comparisons beyond synthetic, single-model, single-budget settings, and test them on realistic agent tasks.", "premises": ["C24", "C23", "C4"], "verdicts": [{"question_id": "paper.inference_follows", "answer": true, "probabilities": null, "confidence": 0.95, "confidence_source": "self_report", "backend": "glm-flash", "escalated": true, "cost_usd": 2.2939e-05, "latency_ms": 2067, "trace_id": "ce07d6b3f78144e4b9c9a471bbb94729", "producer_id": "p3.paper.interpret", "judge_id": "p2.judge"}], "status": "pass", "reason": null}
{"id": "I16", "section": "A research agenda", "text": "Directly test the joint link between codebase scale, context growth and tool attrition, which is stated to lack published empirical tests.", "premises": ["C55", "C22"], "verdicts": [{"question_id": "paper.inference_follows", "answer": true, "probabilities": null, "confidence": 0.9, "confidence_source": "self_report", "backend": "glm-flash", "escalated": true, "cost_usd": 6.263775e-05, "latency_ms": 10600, "trace_id": "30dd7faf450b462ca845a7fa6ef5e1d6", "producer_id": "p3.paper.interpret", "judge_id": "p2.judge"}], "status": "pass", "reason": null}
{"id": "I17", "section": "A research agenda", "text": "Run cross-model and repository-scale validations of governance and architecture claims, since existing validation is preliminary or does not isolate causes.", "premises": ["C57", "C56"], "verdicts": [{"question_id": "paper.inference_follows", "answer": true, "probabilities": null, "confidence": 0.9, "confidence_source": "self_report", "backend": "glm-flash", "escalated": true, "cost_usd": 2.44615e-05, "latency_ms": 3068, "trace_id": "27d8cb965ea74210a2b7a58ff5ff6462", "producer_id": "p3.paper.interpret", "judge_id": "p2.judge"}], "status": "pass", "reason": null}
{"id": "I18", "section": "A research agenda", "text": "Add repeated-use measures such as memory retrieval precision, memory hygiene and minimal-context efficiency to agent benchmarks.", "premises": ["C48"], "verdicts": [{"question_id": "paper.inference_follows", "answer": true, "probabilities": {"true": 0.78, "false": 0.21999999999999997}, "confidence": 0.78, "confidence_source": "logprobs", "backend": "jev", "escalated": false, "cost_usd": 2.0622e-05, "latency_ms": 110, "trace_id": "31514a3066fb49a8b49eedf4b76ddd75", "producer_id": "p3.paper.interpret", "judge_id": "p2.judge"}], "status": "pass", "reason": null}
